# The image is built from this folder, and `next build` traces the whole
# project into the standalone server, so anything left in the build context
# can end up in the image. Leave out secrets, local data, installed packages
# and build or test output; the build installs and builds its own.
# Secrets and databases are left out at any depth (no tracked folder is
# named keys, no tracked file is a .pem, .env or database but .env.example).
.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/keys
**/*.pem
data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
node_modules
.next
out
build
deploy/dist
packages/cli/dist
coverage
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
